WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:02.690
Australia's great Victoria Desert.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:11.330
A featureless expanse of sand hills and
scrub the size of California.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:20.220
Ed Kavanaugh is heading deep into this vast
wilderness drawn by something weird revealed

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.270
from space.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.750
I've lived in Australia my whole life and
never seen anything quite like this before.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:38.150
An image taken over the region on April 8th,
2021, has captured this pattern in the red

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:39.200
sands below.

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:45.860
Out in the middle of nowhere is this giant
carving on the earth.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:48.300
It looks like kind of wedges of a pizza.

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:51.510
It's very strange.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:57.180
The middle of it has been cleared in a way
that it forms almost a bull's eye.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:07.470
The mystery symbol covers an area equivalent
to 600 football fields and has spokes up to

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:09.360
1400 feet in length.

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:18.370
The shape itself has been created with
precision, which can only mean that some sort

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:21.610
of government or military operation has
taken place here.

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:30.300
What's more, the remains of an identical
shape sit nearby.

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:36.220
Great effort appears to have been made to
erase evidence of it.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:42.240
As a journalist, when I see something
clandestine in my own backyard, I feel

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.160
compelled to go and investigate it.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:52.080
Officially, there are no towns near the site.

00:01:54.370 --> 00:01:56.890
But evidence on the ground suggests
otherwise.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:02.260
Wow. This is insane.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:04.510
I mean, this completely deserted ghost town.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:08.390
This can't just be a coincidence.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:17.790
Just 15 miles from the mystery symbols sits
this ghost town.

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:26.320
Dozens of its buildings have been razed to
the ground.

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:29.540
This clearly would have been a very sizeable
community here.

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:31.550
It looks like it's been abandoned for
decades.

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:36.480
Whatever forced this town to flee.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:38.640
It appears to have happened almost
overnight.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:44.350
Oh, this is amazing.

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:48.310
All the chairs and equipment are left
exactly in place, as they would have been

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:49.390
decades ago.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.610
Everyone's just got up and left.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:58.800
In each room, Kavanaugh finds evidence of
government activity.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:01.980
This vehicle was completely out of place
here.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:06.030
It's clearly been modified for some purpose.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:11.340
It's got a completely enclosed cabin to
separate this part of the vehicle from those

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:12.210
who are driving it.

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:19.090
The vehicle appears to be designed to contain
something extremely hazardous.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:26.280
Satellite images of another ghost town in
Australia could offer a clue.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:34.100
What we do know is that a town in Australia
did have to evacuate because of a toxic

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:35.270
asbestos mine.

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:39.650
Could this have been the same case in the
town we're looking at here?

00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:50.590
Between the 1940s and the 1960s, miners in
the town of Wittenoom excavate around 165,000

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:53.440
tonnes of blue asbestos from the desert.

00:03:55.270 --> 00:04:01.310
Over the years, 2000 people die from
unwittingly inhaling the cancerous fibres.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:05.590
Before the government shuts down the mine
and wipes the town off the map.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:12.660
It's actually the largest contaminated site
in the entire southern hemisphere.

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:13.500
That's big.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:21.790
The nightmare scenario is that the ghost town
and the shapes in the image may be evidence

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:25.480
of another equally deadly disaster on
Australian soil.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.880
One that authorities are trying to cover up.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:35.500
Something bad has happened to you to make
people abandon this town.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:39.160
And I'm certain it's got something to do
with those wagon wheel shapes I've seen in

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:39.760
the desert.

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:50.950
The indigenous people here call this area the
big evil.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:55.310
And the journalist soon learns.

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:55.850
Why.

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:02.060
The closer I get to the wagon shapes, the
vegetation is getting thinner and thinner.

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:07.160
It's almost as if some sort of event is
taking place here that is just wiped all of

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.630
the life off the face of the earth.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:20.670
Arriving at the coordinates, Kavner discovers
a vast flat area.

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:30.830
First thing I've noticed is these strange
hooks that are embedded into this concrete

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:39.270
slab. I'm not sure at all what these would
be pinning to the ground, but it certainly

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:40.650
adds to the mystery here.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:48.850
Nearby, Kavner finds more objects not visible
in the satellite image.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:57.720
Wow. Look at this. These look like some sort
of rocket launching devices.

00:05:57.730 --> 00:06:01.300
They're incredibly old and brittle and all
rusted out.

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:09.440
The rocket launchers are weird enough, but
what really intrigues Kavner is what

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:10.370
surrounds them.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:15.950
There's this field of green glass.

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:19.580
It almost looks like a green jade all across
the ground out here.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:27.150
Millions of square feet of desert around the
mystery shapes shimmer with the deformed

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:28.650
beads of glass.

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:38.200
Kavner believes this is trinitite a
substance formed when sand is subjected to

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:41.770
temperatures in excess of 3000°F.

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:48.290
This suggests to me that this has to have
been made from a nuclear weapons test.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:55.060
I must say I'm completely speechless
discovering this year.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:07:02.090
What's concerning is that there are only nine
countries with known nuclear weapons

00:07:02.090 --> 00:07:05.450
capabilities. And Australia isn't one of
them.

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:08.990
The idea is just unfathomable.

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:11.240
But there's just no other explanation.

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:13.130
And it's just completely shocking.

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:15.650
Hey, it's it's Edward Kavanaugh.

00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:21.770
Kavanaugh turns to his newspaper contacts to
track down someone who might be able to shed

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:22.640
some light.

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:23.990
All right. Thanks.

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:32.330
Jeremy Lebois is a member of the Maralinga
Tjarutja, a council of local Aboriginal

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:33.110
peoples.

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:36.410
Hi Jeremy, How are you going?

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:37.010
Good, thanks.

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:45.380
He confirms that 60 years ago atomic testing
did take place in this desert, but not ones

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:47.720
conducted by the Australian Government.

00:07:47.810 --> 00:07:53.510
Where we are today is where the British
tested seven atomic bombs.

00:07:53.510 --> 00:07:56.270
They were bigger than what they dropped on
Japan.

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:05.990
In 1952, the British become the world's third
nuclear power and are desperate to play catch

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:08.060
up with the US and Soviet Union.

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:15.600
To do that, the small, densely populated
nation needs to persuade another country to

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.370
host their nuclear tests.

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:21.990
The British government looked for testing
sites in the US and Canada, but were turned

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:22.590
down.

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:24.810
And then Britain knocked on the door of
Australia.

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:27.060
Part of the old Empire.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:29.430
And the Aussies go, You know what?

00:08:29.430 --> 00:08:30.640
Yeah, we'll have your nukes.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:32.550
Let's blow up some nukes in our deserts.

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:38.470
In exchange for sharing nuclear secrets.

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:43.510
The Australian Government grants the British
vast swaths of land for their tests.

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:47.260
But it's land that belongs to Lebois and his
people.

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:52.630
Jeremy How much notice were the traditional
owners of this land given about the nuclear

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:53.320
tests?

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:55.180
Absolutely nothing.

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:59.590
Not one of them ever, ever sat down with the
traditional owners and asked them for

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:01.510
permission. Not one of them.

